# Scope

This rule applies **only** to this project: the local Feeding App workspace and GitHub repo `hemvanh/feeding-app`. Do not use these branch roles or the **publish all** / **deploy all** phrases in any other repo.

# Branch roles

This repo has two jobs. Do not mix them.

- **`main`**: live GitHub Pages site only. Root is the built `dist` files (`index.html`, `feeding-data.json`, icons). Do not merge source (`src/`, `package.json`, etc.) into `main`.
- **`dev`**: active development with AI. Source of truth for the Vite app. Work, commits, and PRs happen here.

When publishing: `npm run build` on `dev`, then copy `dist` contents onto `main` and commit there. Do not merge `dev` → `main`.

Stay on `dev` unless the user explicitly asks to update the live Pages files on `main`.

# Phrase: "publish all" or "deploy all"

**publish all** and **deploy all** are the same phrase. When the user says either one, do this in order without asking again:

1. On **`dev`**, before any commit: update `.cursor/skills/feeding-app/SKILL.md`, and `reference.md` when data shape, sync, or hosting changed, so the manual matches the latest behavior from this session's changes. Do not publish a skill that still describes the old behavior.
2. On **`dev`**: stage only the relevant source changes, including that skill update, commit, and `git push origin dev`.
3. On **`dev`**: run `npm run build`.
4. Copy built `dist` files onto **`main`** (`index.html`, `favicon.svg`, `icons.svg`, `manifest.json`, `sw.js`, `pwa-icon-192.png`, `pwa-icon-512.png`, `apple-touch-icon.png`, `pwa-icon.svg`). Do **not** overwrite live `feeding-data.json` unless the user asks. Do **not** commit `dist/` or `node_modules/` onto `main`. Do **not** merge `dev` into `main`.
5. Commit and `git push origin main`.
6. Check out **`dev`** again and leave that as the active branch.

Skip an empty `dev` commit if there is nothing to commit; still build and update `main` if the live site needs the latest build.
